{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1794840475","published":"2026-11-16T14:48:09Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:28:37.487723169Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-109261","CVE-2026-109262","CVE-2026-109264","CVE-2026-109276","CVE-2026-116151"],"summary":"Fix of 5 CVEs","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: temporary files left behind by the JNG decoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-109276.patch: remove the color and alpha\n       temporary files in DestroyJNG() in coders/png.c\n     - CVE-2026-109276\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak in the SVG encoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-109262.patch: release the token and primitive\n       buffers before throwing on unbalanced or too deeply nested graphic\n       contexts in WriteSVGImage() in coders/svg.c\n     - CVE-2026-109262\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak in the GIF encoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-109261.patch: release the colormaps and the\n       cloned image info when quantization fails in WriteGIFImage() in\n       coders/gif.c\n     - CVE-2026-109261\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leaks in the JNG encoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116151.patch: release the JPEG image info and\n       the JPEG image on the memory allocation failure paths in\n       WriteOneJNGImage() in coders/png.c\n     - CVE-2026-116151\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: unbounded nesting of image reads from SVG and MVG\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-109264.patch: limit the nesting depth of\n       image reads with a coder_depth field in ImageInfo in magick/image.c,\n       magick/image.h and magick/image-private.h, and read the SVG image\n       element and the MVG image primitive through StrictReadImage(), which\n       refuses explicit coder prefixes other than mpr: and mpri:, in\n       coders/svg.c, magick/draw.c and magick/constitute-private.h\n     - CVE-2026-109264","affected":[{"package":{"name":"imagemagick","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:18.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/imagemagick?distro=ubuntu-18.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","even